  "body": "## What changed\n\n`diag_lines_are_tracing_events_at_their_level` moves from the `diag` unit tests in the `camcraft-ui` lib to a new test binary, `crates/ui/tests/diag_events.rs`. That binary holds this one test only. The test calls `diag::warn` and `diag::info` directly. The lib keeps `the_macros_take_println_shaped_arguments`, which compiles the two macros. The assertions do not change.\n\n## Cause\n\n`tracing` caches the interest of each callsite for the whole process. The test installs a thread-local subscriber with `with_default`. In the lib binary, other tests on other threads call `diag_info!` through the same callsite. If another thread registers the callsite with the dispatchers that it saw before the new subscriber, and that registration ends after the rebuild of the new subscriber, the cached interest is \"never\". The INFO line is then lost and the WARN line (another callsite) stays. This agrees with the output in the issue. No other test in the lib installs a subscriber. In a binary of its own, no other thread uses these callsites.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/2595-diag-events-own-binary.md` (the dropped options: `rebuild_interest_cache()`, a shared lock, a global subscriber).\n\n## Readings (Windows 11, 16 threads)\n\n- `diag_events` binary: 50 runs, 50 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- --test-threads=16`: 3 full runs, each `1251 passed; 0 failed; 7 ignored`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 3 steps, 0 failed (ui build, ui lib, diag_events).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` does not change: one test moves from the lib to the new binary.\n\n## Pinning test\n\n`diag_events::diag_lines_are_tracing_events_at_their_level`\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- I did not reproduce the failure on this machine before the change. The issue measured 1 failure in 3 full lib runs on Linux.\n- No run on Linux or macOS.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #2595\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
